      "message": "@pointbazaar Hello everyone! Two points here:\n\n\u003e why do we need to document it here\n\nBecause others already did. There\u0027s an example of host BIOS configuration, i have added another one. We are new here, so following existing rules assuming they are valid.\n\n\u003e will this config record not be in entity-manager repo already?\n\nSorry, no, because of our client\u0027s NDA policy. They don\u0027t want to publicly display full constitution of their hardware.\n\nWe do have some more sub-components here relying on these changes, we are only uptreaming changes, which affect the code, which is already present in the repo (i. e. spi-flash sub-component), so that it can be used as a framework. We believe it\u0027s useful for others because:\n1. There are more chips out there, which use serial interface with text-based console.\n2. Someone else is probably using Broadcom switches on their CMC boards.",
